{
  "what": "Measured reuse-density profile of the E19 measurement window. karc.bench.e5_killgate._repeat_allocation spreads the r=0.5 reuse budget as [4]*(n/2) + [3]*(n/2) over an n-session build, so a 24-session build carries 4 reuse tasks per session in S01..S12 and 3 in S13..S24. The E19 window S09..S20 therefore contains 4 sessions at 4/7 reuse and 8 at 3/7. E18's 12-session build split 6/6.",
  "why_it_matters": "More reuse means more resident hits, fewer karc MCP round trips, and therefore a lower karc gross. In leg A the four 4/7 sessions have a per-session gross ratio just below 1.0 and the eight 3/7 sessions just above it, so the pooled Q1 result rests on the window's reuse mix. Leg B is above 1.0 in all twelve sessions.",
  "not_a_selection": "The window was fixed before execution (warm-up length 8 forces S09..S20 in a 24-session build) and the two arms see identical tasks in every session, so the pairing is intact. No sub-range of the window is judged, and no alternative pooling is computed - re-slicing is what the preregistration forbids.",
  "disclosed_oversight": "Before fixing the window this profile was not checked. Resident-token disjointness and the resident ramp were checked; reuse density was not.",
